{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You came in tonight because your oxygen dropped at home, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I was on 3 liters and my PCA said my sats were 84%. I felt short of breath and couldn’t cough anything up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You were just discharged two days ago for pneumonia. Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your oxygen is 96% on 4 liters now, heart rate is normal. You’re not in distress here, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do feel a little better since the breathing treatments in the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you got albuterol and lasix. The chest X-ray shows the pneumonia in your right lower lung is still there, but we also see some fluid buildup in the lungs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Fluid? Like heart failure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not exactly. Your heart is enlarged, but this looks more like mild congestion from not clearing secretions well. We gave you a small dose of lasix to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s because I couldn’t cough?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. With your paraplegia, your breathing muscles are weak, so mucus gets stuck. That’s likely what caused the desat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I tried the chest PT my PCA did, but it didn’t help much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll help with that. We started you on guaifenesin to loosen mucus and will use the Acapela and Flutter Vest to help clear it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need that at home too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’re arranging for the vest to be delivered. It’s very important to keep your lungs clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-12-25 21:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-12-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are stable. White count is normal, and your vancomycin level is in the right range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-12-26 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the antibiotic still needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-12-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re continuing vancomycin and Zosyn for two more days to finish the full 8-day course for pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-12-26 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my oxygen? I was on 2 liters before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-12-26 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on 3 liters now, but we’re hopeful you’ll return to 2 liters as the infection clears."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-12-26 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about that high CO2 level I’ve had in the past?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-12-26 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good question. Your bicarbonate is high at 40, which means you retain CO2. You don’t have sleep apnea, but you may need CPAP later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-12-26 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve heard that can help with mucus too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-12-26 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ll refer you for a sleep study after you recover. It could help prevent future episodes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-12-26 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The respiratory therapist used the Flutter Vest and Acapela this morning. How did that feel?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-12-26 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It helped. I was able to cough up some thick mucus after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-12-26 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. That’s exactly what we want. Keep doing that several times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-12-26 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Should my PCA do chest PT too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-12-26 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, manual chest PT is still important, especially in the morning and evening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-12-26 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. Your oxygen is 94% on 3 liters, and you’re breathing comfortably."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Am I going home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you. You’ll finish the IV antibiotics at home with home health support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same PICC line?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the PICC is still in good condition. Home health will give your vancomycin and Zosyn for two more days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the breathing treatments?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue the albuterol as needed, use the Acapela and Flutter Valve four times a day or as needed. The vest will be delivered soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my oxygen at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stay on 3 liters for now. If you feel well, you can try lowering it, but keep sats above 90%. Don’t worry if they’re not perfect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the sleep study?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll notify your pulmonologist to schedule it after you recover. It’s important for long-term breathing support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much more confident now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep up the chest clearance, take your meds, and call if you have trouble breathing or fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-12-27 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-12-25 21:11:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-12-27 17:38:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with T1-T2 paraplegia and chronic restrictive lung disease, was readmitted two days after discharge for desaturation to 84% at home. She had ongoing multifocal pneumonia and developed mild pulmonary vascular congestion, likely due to mucus plugging from impaired cough. She was treated with IV vancomycin and piperacillin-tazobactam, bronchodilators, lasix, and aggressive airway clearance using the Flutter Vest and Acapela. Her respiratory status improved, and she was discharged on day two to complete antibiotics at home. A sleep study was recommended for chronic hypercarbia. Discharge included home oxygen, mucolytics, and respiratory equipment delivery.",
    "problems": [
      "Pneumonia, organism unspecified",
      "Paraplegia",
      "Acidosis",
      "Other fluid overload",
      "Chronic airway obstruction, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism"
    ]
  }
}
